but first all eyes of the world on great  britain queen elizabeth ii has died at  96 years old she ruled for so long most  people of britain have never known  another monarch here's ian lee looking  back at her life  even into her 90s queen elizabeth ii  kept up her royal duties she became the  longest reigning monarch in british  history in 2015. inevitably a long life  can pass by many milestones  my own is no exception  elizabeth alexandra mary windsor was not  in line to be queen but in 1936 the  ten-year-old princess nicknamed lillibet  was put on the fast track after her  uncle king edward viii abdicated to  marry an american divorcee  elizabeth's father became king george vi  then elizabeth became first in line as  her country fought world war ii the  young royal was thrust into another  spotlight  [Music]  she made her first radio broadcast to  our country in 1940 a message of  encouragement to children forced to  leave their homes to escape the dangers  of war and when peace comes  remember  it will be for us the children of today  to make the world of tomorrow a better  and happier place after world war ii in  1947 elizabeth gave england something to  celebrate she married philip mountbatten  a member of the greek royal family the  following year the first of their four  children was born charles the next  prince of wales  her father king george died in 1952.  at 25 years old elizabeth became queen  millions watched the first ever  televised crowning of a british monarch  queen elizabeth worked with more than a  dozen british prime ministers beginning  with winston churchill and was head of  state in 15 other commonwealth countries  a series of royal dramas marked her  reign her son andrew's high-profile  marriage to sarah ferguson failed and in  1992 her oldest son charles separated  from princess diana  that same year the queen watched part of  windsor castle go up in flames  destroying millions in art and furniture  1992  is not a year on which i shall look back  with undiluted pleasure in 1997 a car  crash in paris killed princess diana  stunning the world many criticized the  queen for not showing emotion  more than a decade later the queen  celebrated a royal wedding as her  grandson prince william married kate  middleton the couple gave the queen  three heirs to the throne  her majesty marked 60 years on the  throne in 2012 when a thousand ships  sailed the river thames to honor her and  in 2016 queen elizabeth celebrated her  90th birthday thousands packed the  streets of windsor to catch a glimpse of  the only monarch most had ever known  the queen watched another tiny royal  join the family after her youngest  grandson prince harry married meghan  markle  just a few years later the queen lost  her husband of 73 years she called the  death of prince philip a huge void in  her life but she carried on  and at 96 years old celebrated her  platinum jubilee the week of fanfare and  festivities marked the queen's 70 years  on the british throne  ian lee cbs news london  truly just a remarkable life along with  her grandchildren and great  grandchildren the queen had a lifelong  love of corgi dogs in fact she owned  more than 30 during her reign
 

